{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775377069-z2LduSakC4oISDWz077U","role":"assistant","created":1775377088,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is the 1972 data from April 28, 1972. Let me parse this carefully. The table shows Treasury Bills with their issue dates and amounts outstanding. \n\nFor 13-week bills:\n- Looking at the issue dates in the \"13-week\" column (the third column which shows \"13-week\" issue dates)\n- The first column shows \"Amount outstanding (millions)\" for 13-week bills\n- The second column shows \"Amount outstanding (millions)\" for 26-week bills\n- The third and fourth columns show the issue dates for 13-week and 26-week bills\n\nLet me identify 13-week bills issued during February to April (Feb-Apr) of each year:\n\nFor 1972, looking at the 13-week column (first column for amount, third column for issue date):\n- Row 1: $2,301M, issue date 2/3/72\n- Row 2: $2,301M, issue date 2/10/72\n- Row 3: $2,405M, issue date 2/17/72\n- Row 4: $2,401M, issue date 2/25/72\n- Row 5: $2,401M, issue date 3/2/72\n- Row 6: $2,401M, issue date 3/9/72\n- Row 7: $2,402M, issue date 3/16/72\n- Row 8: $2,401M, issue date 3/23/72\n- Row 9: $2,300M, issue date 3/30/72\n- Row 10: $2,301M, issue date 4/6/72\n- Row 11: $2,301M, issue date 4/13/72\n- Row 12: $2,301M, issue date 4/20/72\n- Row 13: $2,300M, issue date 4/27/72\n\n\n- Row 14: $2,301M, issue date 5/4/72\n\nI'll continue analyzing the bills from February to April 1972. Most 13-week bills during this period have amounts around $2,300-$2,400M, with one notable exception of $2,405M on 2/17/72. I'll track these amounts carefully to understand the Treasury bill issuance patterns.\n\nThe criterion requires identifying bills exceeding $2,400M and issued between February and April. Only the $2,405M bill from 2/17/72 meets both conditions for 1972. I'll methodically examine the subsequent years to find similar patterns.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_5e481ce2dd9c45e1898a2b36","t