ns of USD rounded to the nearest whole number\" might just be a clumsy way of describing the format of the amounts being discussed.\n\n\nI need to check my calculation method. The phrase could also mean to sum the rounded amount in millions for bills exceeding 2400, or maybe sum and then round to nearest whole number million USD. Looking at the example - the issue dates are in February, March, April for each year, and the data shows bills from April 1972 with dates like 2/3/72, 2/10/72, 2/17/72, 2/25/72, 3/2/72 and so on. Let me verify whether I'm pulling all the 13-week bills from those months correctly.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_9e681d176ddbe7aa","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1972_05_page_89.txt | head -50"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
